cal perspective leads a  group of characters to overcome their  hatred for the sake of the common good  and this gets at the coolest thing about  stoicism  it's really a philosophy of life the  stories weren't primarily focused on  heady like making metaphysical arguments  about the nature of being or logically  deliberating on the nature of truth  they think philosophically for the sake  of living a good life  something that puts them in touch with  the spirit of socrates it also makes  them predecessors of the 19th and 20th  century existential philosophers for  whom philosophy is primarily about how  we live life and make sense of our  existence and not merely about how we  understand things in a detached sense  and if you're interested in learning  more about this tradition i can't  recommend pierre hadeau's philosophy as  a way of life highly enough so access  your library card titan and check it out  but what do you guys think can attack on  titan teach us about the virtues of the  stoics  or are we just watching genocidal  maniacs have a field day let us know  what you think in the comments and  definitely let me know if there are  other shows movies or games that you  think warrant some philosophical  attention thanks as always to our  amazing patrons for all your support and  if you haven't checked out our patreon  page in a while we have a lot of great  new content going up so give it a peek  hit that subscribe button like you're  stoically blowing up your own boat and  don't forget to ring that bell as always  thanks for watching later  okay we'll we'll stop that one right  there but um you know not really good  advice for  like how to be a good  brother um i think you know but um i'm  just waiting for the prompter to get  here so they're gonna put this in the  video
 

